diff --git a/docs/figma/hotbar-notes.md b/docs/figma/hotbar-notes.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fed0069
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/figma/hotbar-notes.md
@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+# Hotbar: Figma to Roblox notes
+
+Source: `design/figma/hotbar.json`, from the file "Block Builder - UI" (version 2208815566419836712,
+modified 2026-11-02). Node `31:100` is the "HUD / Desktop" frame and `31:2` is the "Hotbar Slot"
+component set (variants Default `31:3`, Hover `31:4`, Pressed `31:5`, Selected `31:6`). No
+screenshot came with the export, so nothing here has been checked against a picture of the design.
+
+The frame is 1920x1080, which is the project's reference size (`UI/Screen.luau`), so every Figma
+number is used as is.
+
+## Where it lives
+
+| Figma | Roblox |
+|---|---|
+| Color, text, radius, and stroke values | `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/UI/Theme.luau` |
+| Hotbar Slot component set | `UI/HotbarSlot.luau`. Props: `Color`, `Key`, `ShowKey`, `IsSelected`. Hover and Pressed follow the pointer (`GuiState`) |
+| HUD / Desktop: Selected Name and Hotbar | `UI/Hotbar.luau` (same props and behavior as before) |
+| Previews | `src/ServerScriptService/Stories/UI/HotbarSlot.story` and `Hotbar.story` (UI Labs) |
+
+Everything is drawn with UI instances. Nothing needed to be exported as an image.
+
+## What Roblox can't reproduce exactly
+
+| Design | What Roblox does instead | What it looks like |
+|---|---|---|
+| Selected Name font: **Gilroy ExtraBold** (800) | **Montserrat ExtraBold**. Roblox ships no Gilroy and doesn't load custom fonts | A similar geometric sans. Montserrat runs slightly wider |
+| Selected Name **letter spacing -0.5** | Left out. Roblox text has no letter spacing | Letters sit about half a pixel further apart, so "Window" is roughly 3 px wider |
+| Selected Name **outside text stroke**, 2 px, black at 60% | `UIStroke` (Contextual), thickness 2, transparency 0.4 | Roblox draws its own text outline, so check that the thickness looks the same |
+| Hotbar **opacity 80%** on the whole frame, slots included | 0.8 is multiplied into every fill, stroke, and text inside the bar (`Theme.fade`). A `CanvasGroup` would fade it as one picture, but it costs texture memory on an always-on HUD and makes text slightly soft | Each layer fades on its own and they stack. The bar alone is 80% opaque as designed, but a slot drawn over the bar is about 96% opaque, so less of the world shows through the slots than in Figma: over a bright sky a slot comes out up to about 30 RGB steps darker. If that matters, wrapping the bar in a `CanvasGroup` with `GroupTransparency = 0.2` (and setting `Theme.HotbarOpacity` to 1) matches Figma exactly |
+| Hotbar **stroke on the top side only** (2 px, white at 12%, inside) | A 2 px line across the straight part of the top edge, inset by the 14 px corner radius at each end. `UIStroke` always draws all four sides | The highlight stops where the corners start curving. Figma carries it a little way around the corners, thinning as it goes |
+| Slot **smoothed corners** (radius 12, smoothing 60%) | `UICorner` with radius 12, which draws a plain circular corner | The corners look a little sharper where they meet the straight edges. A 9-slice image would match exactly, but it wasn't worth it for a 64 px tile |
+| Selected **gradient stroke** outside, 3 px, #FFD25A to #FF801A left to right | `UIStroke` (outer, 3 px) with a `UIGradient` (rotation 0) | Should match. Check it on screen |
+| **Pressed** variant is a 60x60 slot | The slot keeps its 64x64 place in the bar and its face shrinks to 60x60 around the center (swatch 40 to 36, badge inset 4 to 3) | In Figma's auto layout, a 60 px slot would pull its neighbors 4 px closer. Keeping the place stops the bar jumping on every tap, and the hit area stays under the finger |
+
+## States the design doesn't show
+
+These are built from the design's own values. Please review them:
+
+- **Selected and hovered or pressed at once.** The design has no variant for both. The slot takes
+  the hover or pressed fill and size and keeps the selected outline.
+- **Motion.** The design has no prototype transitions, so state changes are instant.
+- **Show Key = false.** The prop exists (`ShowKey`) and hides the badge, but the hotbar always shows
+  the keys, as before. Hiding them on touch screens, where there are no number keys, would be a
+  design decision.
+- **Block transparency.** Window and Ice blocks are see-through in the world, but their swatches are
+  solid, as before and as the design shows.
+
+## Things to check on screen
+
+No screenshot came with the export, and the build hasn't been run in Studio. Please look at:
+
+1. The Selected Name in Montserrat against Gilroy in Figma, including its outline.
+2. The top highlight on the bar, and whether it is too faint at 0.12 x 0.8.
+3. The selected outline's gradient direction (yellow on the left, orange on the right).
+4. Hover and press on a slot with a mouse, and press with a finger on a touch device.
+5. **Phones.** The design has only a desktop frame. At 732 px the bar is wider than most phone
+   screens in landscape, and it overlaps Roblox's thumbstick and jump button. The old 630 px bar had
+   the same problem. A phone layout (smaller slots or two rows) needs a design.
+
+## Measured against the design (by the numbers)
+
+At 1920x1080 the layout code places these boxes, which match the Figma boxes:
+
+| Layer | Figma box (x, y, w, h) | Roblox |
+|---|---|---|
+| Hotbar | 594, 972, 732, 84 | Centered, bottom 24 px up, 732x84 from 10 slots x 64 + 9 gaps x 8 + 2 x 10 padding |
+| Selected Name | centered, y 936, height 28 | Centered, 28 tall, 8 px above the bar |
+| First slot | 604, 982, 64, 64 | 10 px padding, then 72 px apart |
+| Swatch | 12 px in, 40x40 | Centered in the 64 px slot |
+| Key Badge | 4 px in, 18x18 | 4 px in, 18x18, round |
+
+These come from the code, not from a running game. Measure `AbsolutePosition` and `AbsoluteSize` in
+a playtest at 1920x1080 to confirm them.
